      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let's solve the problem step by step.\n\nGiven that \\(10, a, b, ab\\) is an arithmetic progression, we know that the difference between consecutive terms is constant. Therefore, we can write the following equation:\n\\[a - 10 = b - a = ab - b.\\]\n\nLet's denote this common difference by \\(d\\). Then we have:\n\\[a - 10 = d,\\]\n\\[b - a = d,\\]\n\\[ab - b = d.\\]\n\nFrom the first two equations, we can express \\(b\\) in terms of \\(a\\):\n\\[b = a + d,\\]\n\\[b = a - d.\\]\nSince both expressions are equal to \\(b\\), we can set them equal to each other:\n\\[a + d = a - d.\\]\nSolving for \\(d\\), we get:\n\\[d = -a - d \\implies 2d = -a \\implies d = -\\frac{a}{2}.\\]\nSubstituting \\(d = -\\frac{a}{2}\\) into the first equation, we get:\n\\[a - 10 = -\\frac{a}{2} \\implies a + \\frac{a}{2} = 10 \\implies \\frac{3a}{2} = 10 \\implies a = \\frac{20}{3}.\\]\n\nNow, we can find \\(d\\):\n\\[d = -\\frac{a}{2} = -\\frac{\\frac{20}{3}}{2} = -\\frac{10}{3}.\\]\n\nNext, we need to find \\(b\\):\n\\[b = a + d = \\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{10}{3} = \\frac{10}{3}.\\]\n\nFinally, we need to verify that \\(b\\) and \\(ab\\) along with \\(a\\) and \\(d\\) satisfy the arithmetic progression condition. We have:\n\\[ab = \\left(\\frac{20}{3}\\right)\\left(\\frac{10}{3}\\right) = \\frac{200}{9},\\]\nand\n\\[d = ab - b = \\frac{200}{9} - \\frac{10}{3} = \\frac{200}{9} - \\frac{30}{9} = \\frac{170}{9}.\\]\n\nWe can check if \\(a, b, ab, d\\) form an arithmetic progression:\n\\[a - 10 = \\frac{20}{3} - 10 = \\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{30}{3} = -\\frac{10}{3},\\]\n\\[b - a = \\frac{10}{3} - \\frac{20}{3} = -\\frac{10}{3},\\]\n\\[ab - b = \\frac{200}{9} - \\frac{10}{3} = \\frac{200}{9} - \\frac{30}{9} = \\frac{170}{9},\\]\n\\[d = -\\frac{10}{3}.\\]\n\nSince all these differences are equal to \\(-\\frac{10}{3}\\), the terms \\(10, \\frac{20}{3}, \\frac{10}{3}, \\frac{200}{9}\\) indeed form an arithmetic progression.\n\nTherefore, the number of pairs \\((a, b)\\) of real numbers that satisfy the condition is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).",
